---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import FeatureVisual from '../../components/FeatureVisual.astro';
import LaunchKibo from '../../components/LaunchKibo.astro';
import { locales, languageTag, origin } from '../../lib/publication.mjs';
const alternates = [...locales.map(locale => ({ lang: languageTag[locale], href: `${origin}/${locale}/kibo/` })), { lang:'x-default', href:`${origin}/zh-hans/kibo/` }];
---
<Base locale="en" title="Azur Promilia Kibo: 24 Official Names & Launch Artwork" description="Browse 18 official Kibo introduction images and six name-only previews from China’s launch website. Original Chinese names, regional groups and source dates included." alternates={alternates}>
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">Home</a><span>/</span>Kibo</nav>
    <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">OFFICIAL KIBO REFERENCES</p><h1>Azur Promilia Kibo names &amp; artwork</h1><p>Match Kibo names and appearances from the official regional website, then check how rewards and acquisition conditions differ.</p></header>
    <FeatureVisual id="kibo-companions" locale="en" priority/>
    <LaunchKibo locale="en"/>
    <section class="prose kibo-next" data-pagefind-body>
      <h2>Are these Kibo newly added after launch?</h2><p>The images and names were checked on November 27, 2026. The showcase does not provide a release date for each Kibo. Finding a missing entry here does not establish that the game added it after the November 26 launch. The count describes this website section, not the total number of Kibo in the game.</p>
      <h2>Are Starry reward Kibo separate species?</h2><p>Japan’s launch reward references include <span lang="ja">星彩・クロディーメ</span> and <span lang="ja">星彩・キラミィ</span>. Those are regional reward names. We keep them separate from the Chinese showcase rather than infer a translation or count each special form as another species. Check the <a href="/en/guides/resources/">reward guide</a> for event and account requirements before attempting a claim.</p>
      <h2>How do capture cards and eggs work?</h2><p>Use the <a href="/en/systems/kibo/">Kibo capture, egg and event guide</a> to compare current prompts, attributed Korean player reports and regional claim rules. For assigned companions, read <a href="/en/systems/home/">farm seeds, jobs and food</a> before filling every station.</p><h2>Can I use a beta community database for launch?</h2><p>First check the database’s version notice. A large list may still contain test-build names, evolution stages or special forms. It can help you identify a question, but a launch acquisition route needs current regional evidence. We have not verified catch coordinates, evolution requirements, farm-work values or breeding combinations for these entries.</p>
      <p>For more source-dated classification and lore references, browse <a href="/ja/kibo/" lang="ja">日本語</a> or <a href="/zh-hans/kibo/" lang="zh-Hans">简体中文</a>. To distinguish companions from characters and anima, start with the <a href="/en/characters/">character roster</a> and <a href="/en/guides/banner-rules/">regional banner guide</a>. An anima appearing beside a character in a banner is not a Kibo.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose"><h2>Travelling with Kibo in artwork</h2><p>A nighttime gathering of characters and Kibo. Use the catalog above to compare names and appearances, or read the <a href="/en/systems/kibo/">Kibo acquisition guide</a> for capture, egg and event distinctions.</p><FeatureVisual id="kibo-night" locale="en"/></section>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>.kibo-next { max-width:850px; padding-bottom:4rem; }</style>
